            <ArticleTitle>Selective coronary arteriography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>377-82</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of 414 selective coronary arteriographies in 322 patients has been done at Ullevål Hospital from May 1971 to Jan. 1974. Judkins technique was used in all cases. The indications for arteriography, the diagnoses as regards the coronary arteries, the therapeutic consequences,and the complications of selective coronary arteriography are described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
